; Where each shot of the recording scene stands (see ShotMarker). The targets are the points the shots look at. The recording has four shots: ShotRecording (A: the hidden camera, east-south-east
; of the shelter, behind ferns, locked; on her left, so that she turns away from it), the strips of ground WalkStart to WalkEnd and Walk2Start to Walk2End (B: the carried camera walks them, pitched at the ground) and ShotRecordingC to CreepEnd (C: someone looking in on the bloody
; shelter from the forest, west of it, creeping closer).
